      },
      "text": "revenue - North / LargeAppliances / Marketplace / Consumer, week ending 2026-08-09.\n\nMovement: 1.0% week-on-week, but -1.8% against forecast - the difference is seasonality that was already expected.\nLocalisation: 72.9% of the shortfall sits in a single slice.\nDecomposition: volume effect dominates (units -20.9%, ASP 4.5%) - not a pricing problem.\n\nCause accepted: Logistics vendor switched (3PL contract change), effective 2026-07-27.\n  Effect: +10.07pp on cancellation_rate, worth Rs 42.6L per week.\n  Survived 6 falsification tests.\n\nRejected, with reasons:\n  - List price increase +3%: temporal precedence violated: the effect began 2026-08-02 but the cause began 2026-08-03 (0 weeks later). A cause cannot post-date its effect.\n  - Competitor promotional sale: dose-response inverted: exposure is highest in West (intensity 1.00) but the effect is concentrated in North (intensity 0.60); correlation between exp\n\nRecommended bundle: Targeted price rollback on Large Appliances, Exit marketplace for Large Appliances in North; route to own-site fulfilment with company-controlled deli\n  Cost Rs 67.0L against an envelope of Rs 70.0L; expected recovery Rs 35.5L per week.\n  Runner-up: Exit marketplace for Large Appliances in North; route to own-site fulfilment with company-controlled delivery at Rs 55.0L recovering Rs 33.0L per week - rejected on value per rupee.\n\nConfidence: 0.63 (confident). One explanation survived all falsification tests and accounts for 63% of the movement.\nUnexplained: Rs 25.1L per week remains unattributed and is NOT covered by the accepted cause.\n  Next test: These metrics cannot support a weekly claim at their native grain; interpolating them would present interpolation as evidence."
    }
